      "document_name": "os_races.md",
      "page": 1,
      "text": "Xv6 has two types of locks: spinlocks and sleep-locks. We’ll start with spinlocks. Xv6 represents a spinlock as a struct spinlock. The important field in the structure is locked, a word that is zero when the lock is available and non-zero when it is held. Were there no concurrency, xv6 could acquire a lock with code like\n\nUnfortunately, this implementation does not guarantee mutual exclusion in the face of concurrency. Two CPUs could simultaneously reach line 25, see that lk->locked is zero, and then both grab the lock by executing line 26. At this point, two different CPUs hold the lock, which violates the mutual exclusion property. What we need is a way to make lines 25 and 26 execute as an atomic (indivisible) step.",
